meta {
  name: GET all partners — see normalised data
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/odata/v4/orders/BusinessPartners
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:4004
}

docs {
  ## Slide 8 wrap-up — confirm the database only holds normalised data

  Read all partners to confirm the record written by the previous request
  really landed as canonical form:

  - `name` is `'ACME CORP'` — not the `'acme corp'` the client sent
  - `country` is `'US'` — not `'us'`

  The client sent mixed-case values. The database received canonical form.
  That gap is what req.data mutation gives you — the whole chapter in one
  GET request.
}
